WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:05.750
So we had the volar hearings today, uh, in
the Mueller hearings.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:11.129
We didn't get anything new about what Donald
Trump did, actions by Trump and the people

00:00:11.129 --> 00:00:12.129
around him.

00:00:12.129 --> 00:00:17.330
But we did get some on the record confirmation
from Robert Mueller about the obstructive,

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:21.780
um, goals and ambitions that Donald Trump
had in his actions.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:26.200
Now, with regard to impeachment after this
is all said and done, after Robert Mueller

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.430
has done testifying, which is still happening
as of the taping of this segment, there will

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:35.240
be people who say, now it's time for an impeachment.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:40.840
There will be some who will say, now it's
time for the actual impeachment and removal

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.940
of Donald Trump from the White House.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.510
There will be others who will say, let's not
impeach.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.420
Let's not even do the inquiry.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.280
Question one is what will Republicans think?

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.540
The answer is actually who cares?

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.329
The important part is what do Democrats think?

00:00:57.329 --> 00:01:03.130
And there is this growing problem of division
within the Democratic Party on the topic of

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.130
impeachment.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.430
There are those in the Democratic Party who
are actually going so far as to say, not only

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:10.970
should Trump be impeached, but there is evidence
for a conviction and removal on the basis

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.450
of that impeachment based on what we know.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:18.490
There are those in the Democratic Party who
say we should do an impeachment inquiry and

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:25.200
let the inquiry take us to either impeaching
or not impeaching but let's start the inquiry

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.200
right away.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.830
And then there are also Democrats who have
publicly said, we shouldn't get involved in

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:33.700
this either for political reasons or because
they don't think that the evidence we've seen

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.799
so far justifies an impeachment inquiry.

00:01:35.799 --> 00:01:40.390
There is a movement within the Democratic
Party to do nothing when it comes to impeachment

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.240
or an impeachment inquiry.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.960
The bottom line is that it's time for Democrats
to cut the crap.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:50.159
And what I mean by that is that if the infighting
about impeachment, if the debate within the

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:54.950
Democratic Party about whether to even have
an impeachment inquiry continues much longer,

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:59.960
it's going to get Trump reelected in 2020,
uh, as are other types of democratic infighting

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:00.960
potentially.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.930
Uh, as I've pointed out before, there are
three options and democrats should figure

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:10.000
out like today which one it is, that they're
going to get behind it.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.690
They need to unite behind it and they need
to carry it out.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:18.910
Any, anything else is going to be damaging
to Democrats in 2020, both, uh, for the removal

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.540
of Donald Trump and also in many of their
own races.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.290
Option number one, start an impeachment inquiry.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:26.980
Right now you don't go directly to impeachment.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.840
You've got to first do the inquiry.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.090
Uh, I would support the decision to start
an impeachment inquiry.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.090
Right now.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.340
I think there is more than enough evidence
to justify the inquiry starting right away.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:44.879
Option two, which I would also support, would
be to decide we're going to table this for

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:50.629
now and started impeachment inquiry in six
months or some number of months in order to

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:54.190
be more damaging to Donald Trump's 2020 reelection
campaign.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.130
Uh, it will become a distraction.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.440
It will interfere with Donald Trump's campaigning.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.560
I would support that.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:05.190
Yes, as I said on Monday, I believe that it
is totally reasonable at this point in time,

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:09.080
given the politics that have been played by
the other side on this issue.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.320
I think it would be completely reasonable
to say, let's do the impeachment inquiry,

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.099
but let's wait a little bit and time it so
as to be the most damaging to Donald Trump

00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:18.099
as possible.

00:03:18.099 --> 00:03:19.480
I would support that as well.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:24.770
Option number three would be to decide today
we are not going to pursue an impeachment

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:25.770
inquiry.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.950
We are going to be done with it and we are
going to move on a period.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:35.090
I don't love it in the sense that I think
the evidence warrants an impeachment inquiry

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:39.040
and an impeachment inquiry could be damaging
to the president in terms of his 2020 reelection

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:45.709
chances, but I would be okay and I would still
sort of uh, get behind.

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:49.950
I would accept the decision to say we are
not going to do anything with an impeachment

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.620
inquiry and we're going to focus on the 2020
election.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:59.860
What cannot be an option is to continue in
fighting for the rest of the 2020 campaign

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.209
about whether or not to do an impeachment
inquiry.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:05.480
That is a loser's game.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.280
Democrats don't be losers.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.680
You lose all the time.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:13.010
We continue to lose even though the American
public is as left as it has ever been.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:17.089
Our elected officials continue pulling, pulling,
pulling to the right.

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:18.089
Yes.

00:04:18.089 --> 00:04:21.699
Partially because of voter suppression, partially
because of Gerrymandering, but also because

00:04:21.699 --> 00:04:24.819
of the self-inflicted damage that Democrats
do.

00:04:24.819 --> 00:04:29.210
There is a lot to gain with an impeachment
inquiry, which we'll push the content of the

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.740
Mueller report into the mainstream.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:36.479
There is nothing to gain from just arguing
about whether or not to do the inquiry.

00:04:36.479 --> 00:04:37.629
It's been long enough.

00:04:37.629 --> 00:04:42.009
If you still don't think the inquiry is warranted
based on the facts you're not going to six

00:04:42.009 --> 00:04:45.770
months from now, uh, there's nothing else
that will change your mind.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:52.759
Please stop the self destructive stuff and
just decide and agree to stop the public disagreements

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:53.759
about it.

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:58.099
Mueller has testified he's almost done with
this, with his test, the testimony.

00:04:58.099 --> 00:05:01.110
You've got to decide on this and move forward
one way or the other.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.110
Let me know what you think.

